    </nav>

    @* Everything the linkshell OWNS, as opposed to Management, which is its people. Gil and Items
       belong together: an item is unsold value and gil is realised value, and selling one turns it
       into the other in a single transaction.

       Both are readable by every member. A treasury only officers can see is how arguments start, and
       member-visible history is the compensating control for there being no second signature on a
       recording. Only changing things needs a permission — CanManageTreasury for gil,
       CanManageInventory for items. *@
    <nav class="nav-section">
        <div class="nav-label">Treasury</div>

        <button type="button" class="nav-item nav-group @IsExpanded("ManageFinances", "ManageRevenue")" data-target="#nav-gil">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"><path d="M12 2v20M17 6H9a3 3 0 0 0 0 6h6a3 3 0 0 1 0 6H6"/></svg>
            Gil
